  "Question": "Of 10 products, 4 are defective. If 3 are drawn without replacement, what is the probability that all 3 are defective?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1/30",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "$C(4,3)\\times C(6,0)/120=4/120=1/30$.\n\nAlternative method 1: Multiply successive defective-draw probabilities\n\nFor uniform random sampling without replacement, all three items are defective exactly when each successive draw is defective. After each such draw, one defective item and one item overall have been removed, so the successive probabilities are \\(\\frac4{10}\\), \\(\\frac39\\), and \\(\\frac28\\). By the probability multiplication rule,\n\\[\nP(\\text{all three defective})\n=\\frac4{10}\\cdot\\frac39\\cdot\\frac28\n=\\frac1{30}.\n\\]",
